     "type": "application",
     "title": "Draft Your Own SFD This Week",
     "content": "Pick one real, currently pending message or conversation that you have been avoiding or rehearsing anxiously - an email, a piece of feedback, a difficult ask. Write the full SFD version privately: every ounce of blame, sarcasm, and score-settling you actually feel, with no editing and no audience. Do not send it, do not read it to anyone, just get it fully onto the page.\n\nSeparately, on its own line, name the story you are making up about the other person or the situation, using the exact phrase: 'the story I'm making up is...' Then list two other plausible explanations for their behavior that have nothing to do with malice or incompetence - genuinely try to generate two, not one, since the first alternative is often just a softer version of the original story.\n\nNow write the final version you will actually send or say, and hold it to four concrete criteria: it leads with curiosity rather than accusation, it states exactly one fact rather than an interpretation, it asks one real question you don't already know the answer to, and it cuts every line whose only function is to score a point. If a sentence would not survive being read aloud to the person's face, it does not survive the revision. Send or say only that final version, and notice how different the outcome is from where the SFD started.",
